# A string is immutable, so `s[i] = c` is refused. Pinned because this arm used
# to be the catch-all for every non-array index-assign and named "strings and
# bytes" whatever the base actually was — a soa hit it and sent readers looking
# for a string that was not there. The message must name ITS OWN subject.
# expect: cannot index-assign an element of string (it is immutable)
fn main():
    s := "abc"
    s[0] = 122
